<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>InfoCarrier.Core</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>InfoCarrier.Core</AssemblyName>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>

    <!--
      Transitive pinning is OFF for the shipped packages, and only for them (M8-21).
      `CentralPackageTransitivePinningEnabled` in Directory.Packages.props promotes a pin into the
      nuspec, so `InfoCarrier.Core` declared `Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection >= 10.0.9`
      although no project references it — a constraint nobody chose, imposed on every consumer.
      The pin exists for the TEST AND SAMPLE restore graph (EF Core's SQLite package floors
      Microsoft.Extensions.Logging at 10.0.9, and without the pin those projects fail NU1109), and
      those projects keep it. A package should declare what it references and nothing else.
    -->
    <CentralPackageTransitivePinningEnabled>false</CentralPackageTransitivePinningEnabled>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="PACKAGE.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="README.md" />
    <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\..\docs\assets\icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="icon.png" Visible="false" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" />

    <!--
      THE RELATIONAL HALF LIVES IN `Relational/` AND THIS IS ITS REFERENCE (D3 superseded
      2026-09-03). It was a separate package until then. The measurements behind the reversal are in
      `docs/architecture.md` §6a: +0.62 MB brotli on a Blazor client, unconditional, no new package
      dependencies, against 262 of 20,368 tests lost without it.

      A FUTURE SPLIT IS A FOLDER MOVE. Everything that needs this reference is under `Relational/`
      and keeps the `InfoCarrier.Core.Relational` namespace, so extracting it again means moving one
      directory and this one line. The supersession lists the three measurable conditions that would
      call for that.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Relational" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
